To turn this mock-up into a colorful website, you can use HTML and CSS to create a webpage with the jokes displayed in a more visually appealing way. You can use JavaScript to replace the jokes with two real jokes. Here is a simple example of the HTML and CSS:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        .joke-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            margin: 0.75rem auto;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="joke-container">
        <p>Isaama . . .</p>
        <p>Bat to a moral punchline . . .</p>
    </div>
    <div class="joke-container">
        <p>Really dumb joke . . .</p>
        <p>Epithet to a real punchline . . .</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```
And here is a simple example of the JavaScript:
```javascript
// Replace the jokes with real jokes
const joke1 = "Isaama . . .";
const joke2 = "Bat to a moral punchline . . .";
const joke3 = "Really dumb joke . . .";
const joke4 = "Epithet to a real punchline . . .";

document.querySelector(".joke-container").innerHTML = joke1;
document.querySelector(".joke-container").innerHTML = joke2;
```
This is just a simple example, and you can further enhance the webpage by adding CSS styles, animations, and JavaScript functionality.

To create a colorful and interactive website with the joke replaced by a real joke, you can use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. First, create a basic HTML structure with two `<div>` elements, each containing a `<span>` element with the text "My Joke Website" and "Funny Joke (Push to reveal punchline?)". Then, add CSS styles to make the text look like a blue box. Finally, use JavaScript to replace the joke with a real joke when the user clicks on the "Funny Joke (Push to reveal punchline?)" text. Here's a basic example:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <style>
        .box {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 10px;
            border: 1px solid black;
            background-color: white;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="box">
        <span>My Joke Website</span>
    </div>
    <div class="box">
        <span>Funny Joke (Push to reveal punchline?)</span>
    </div>
    <script>
        // Replace the joke with a real joke when the user clicks on the "Funny Joke (Push to reveal punchline?)" text
        const funnyJokeSpan = document.querySelector('span:nth-child(2)');
        funnyJokeSpan.addEventListener('click', () => {
            funnyJokeSpan.textContent = "Why did the tomato turn red?";
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```
Remember to replace the joke with a real joke, and you can use a joke API or a database of jokes to achieve this.
